  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Lengthy run of dry and mild weather continues \ninto early November before coming to an end by late next week \n\nAnother day of mainly clear skies with light winds today as high\npressure remains in place across the region. Most locations \nwill see high temperatures this afternoon in the mid to upper \n50s, though parts of south-central PA should reach the low 60s. \nWith model soundings showing a layer of dry air above a weak \ninversion, expect dew points to drop somewhat this afternoon. \nThe magnitude of the drop remains uncertain, but we should see \nRH values fall into the 35 to 45 percent range. \n\nDry weather continues for Sunday though mid and high clouds will\nbe on the increase thanks to an area of warm advection\nassociated with a weak shortwave approaching from the west.\nMoisture appears to be very limited with this disturbance as it\nmoves through on Monday, so we will continue to show a dry \nforecast. Upper level ridging builds back into the region for \nthe first half of the week, helping to prolong our dry stretch \nand keeping high temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above normal for \nmuch of the coming week.\n\nChances for widespread rainfall return for the end of the week\nas a complex system develops over the middle of the country.\nThere is still a lot of uncertainty regarding the evolution of\nthe upper air pattern that will lead to the development of this\nsystem, but confidence continues to increase in our dry streak\ncoming to and end by Thursday and Friday.",
